      "escalated": false,
      "escalation": null,
      "final_text": "The key-value server and its tests are both in the shared repo, and my test push landed at tip 2 after the tester ran it. I didn't run `python -m pytest -q` myself; the tester's `-x` run on my push is the only test result I have. @a1 wrote `kv_server.py`, which I read through and didn't change. I wrote `tests/test_kv.py`.\n\nMy first push of a server was rejected because `kv_server.py` already existed, so I dropped it.\n\nThe tests start a server on port 0 in a thread and cover the following:\n- GET, PUT and DELETE on a key, and the sorted key listing at `/kv`.\n- TTL expiry: a key disappears from GET, the listing and DELETE, an expired key counts as new on the next PUT, and a PUT replaces the ttl.\n- Bad PUT bodies, invalid JSON, wrong paths and wrong methods.\n- Two servers having separate stores.\n\nNo review from another agent is waiting on me.",
